-- Using a file after close() must error at runtime.
--
-- The path comes from `Os.tmpname()` **on purpose**. This fixture first used
-- `/tmp/saule_io_use_after_close.txt`, which does not exist on Windows, so
-- `Io.open` returned nil, the `!` unwrapped it, and the run died at line 4
-- with "force-unwrapped a `nil` value" — never reaching the close, let alone
-- the use after it. It passed the harness the whole time, because
-- `run_tests.sh` gates on exit status and any error will do.
--
-- The fix for that was a *relative* path, which traded the Windows bug for a
-- quieter one: the harness runs from the repo root, so every test run dropped
-- `saule_io_use_after_close.tmp` there and left the working tree dirty (the
-- file was even committed once). `Os.tmpname()` is cross-platform and lands
-- outside the repo, which is what both versions actually wanted.

class Main
	static fn main()
		local f: File = Io.open(Os.tmpname(), IoMode.Write)!
		f.write("hi\n")
		f.close()
		f.write("oops")
	end
end
